{
  "produced_by": "voice_agent",
  "source_narration_script": "That pile of paper on your desk has been growing for weeks. It nags every time you look. Every organizing expert says the same thing. Group like with like. Label everything. Give everything a permanent home. But that pile is already smarter than any filing system you could build. Watch how you use it. Every page you pull out, you drop back on top. What you touch often rises. What you never need sinks. Computers manage memory exactly this way. It's provably about the best you can do without seeing the future. A full sort costs hours to save seconds you'll hardly ever need. Your mess was already a system.",
